Package: omx-plugins
Section: metapackages
Architecture: any
Depends: omx-plugins-clap (= ${binary:Version}), omx-plugins-lv2 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenMixer console effects as CLAP and LV2 plugins (metapackage)
 omx delay, omx drive, omx eq8 and omx strip, in both plugin formats: this
 package installs omx-plugins-clap and omx-plugins-lv2. The DSP inside each
 plugin is the OpenMixer console's own (omx-dsp, linked in statically), so a
 plugin sounds the same in a DAW as on the desk, sample for sample.

Package: omx-plugins-clap
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenMixer console effects as CLAP plugins
 omx delay, omx drive, omx eq8 and omx strip as CLAP plugins, in
 /usr/lib/clap where CLAP hosts find them. The DSP inside each one is the
 OpenMixer console's own (omx-dsp, linked in statically), so a plugin sounds
 the same in a DAW as on the desk, sample for sample.

Package: omx-plugins-lv2
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenMixer console effects as LV2 plugins
 omx delay, omx drive, omx eq8 and omx strip as LV2 plugins, in /usr/lib/lv2
 where LV2 hosts (Ardour, Carla, MOD, Zynthian) find them, with a MOD GUI
 where the plugin declares one. The DSP inside each one is the OpenMixer
 console's own (omx-dsp, linked in statically), so a plugin sounds the same
 in a DAW as on the desk, sample for sample.
